                <pb facs="0471" n="1431" sameAs="frus:frus1888p2/pg1431"/>

                <head>No. 977.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Curry to Mr. Bayard.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Madrid</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1887-12-22"><hi rendition="#italic">December</hi> 22, 1887</date>.
                        (Received January 3, 1888.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 290.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: On receipt of your telegram I at once
                    sought an interview with the minister of state, and he agreed to prolong the
                    commercial agreement <pb facs="0472" n="1432" xml:id="pg1432"/> until June 30,
                    1888. The result was cabled “Agreement prolonged six months.” I now have the
                    honor of inclosing the protocol as signed by Mr. Moret and myself.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">J. L. M. Curry.</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d264-a1.xml" xpointer="d264-a1"/>
            </div>
